# Supabase Pipelines

## Security

- **RLS on every user table** — no `USING (true)` for authenticated write paths unless explicitly justified in an ADR.
- Service role keys stay server-side / Edge Functions only — never in Angular bundles.
- Guest mode: read public/catalog data only; no cross-user vault access (see `@docs/01-master-prd.md`).

## Validation

- Validate all Edge Function / RPC inputs with **Zod** (or agreed schema lib) at the boundary.
- Reject unknown fields; return typed error shapes the client can map.

## Ingestion & AI cache

- Cron / scheduled ingestion pipelines: idempotent upserts keyed by stable external IDs.
- Groq (or AI) responses: cache by **SHA-256** of the canonical prompt + model id + relevant build fingerprint (see `@docs/03-ai-gameplay-agent.md`).
- Cache hits must not re-bill; store hash, model, created_at, and payload (or storage pointer).

## Migrations

- One concern per migration; never edit applied migrations — add a new one.
- Document RLS policy intent in migration comments when non-obvious.

If `supabase/` is missing, scaffold only what the task requires and update `@docs/02-data-schema.md` + `tasks.md`.
